#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0503 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution (review H2): a column that ends in SDT is governed by the longest published stem, *SDT, never by *DT - var_name(\"LIBRARY\") is *SDT, so CDISC-AD0503 does not judge it and only CDISC-AD0509 does (its own invalid scenario). RANDSDT carries a label without 'Date' on purpose: under the retired ends_with-only shape this rule fired on it beside AD0509, a double report under a second id. XDT is the positive control: governed by *DT, its label contains 'Date'."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *DT name=*DT label="{Date}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *SDT name=*SDT label="{Start Date}"
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col XDT type=Char label="Analysis Date"
col RANDSDT type=Char label="Foo"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | x | y
---
